\f0\fs24 \cf0 Baltic Sea phytoplankton dataset\
\
-Harmonisation of the dataset was first described in Olli et al (2013): 
\i\b Harmonising large data sets reveals novel patterns in the Baltic Sea phytoplankton community structure
\i0\b0 , Marine Ecology Progress Series, 473, 53-66. Certain number of samples, and rare species are excluded. For full dataset, contact riina.klais@ut.ee\
\
-Functional trait table is continuously updated by the authors, for the latest version, visit http://www.riinaklais.com\
\

\b Data format
\b0 : .RData file. If you need the data in another data format (txt, xls), contact riina.klais@ut.ee\
\
\
The data file contains 3 tables: abundances of individual taxa in samples (
\i count.table
\i0 ), metadata of the samples (
\i sample.table
\i0 ), and the taxonomy and functional trait values of 679 phytoplankton taxa (
\i phytoplankton.traits
\i0 ).\
\
-
\i sample.table
\i0  and 
\i count.table
\i0  are cross indexed with \'93sampleID\'94 and \'93samplingID\'94 (see below).\
\
-
\i count.table 
\i0 and 
\i phytoplankton.traits 
\i0 are cross indexed with \'93valid_name\'94\
\
count.table\
1) samplingID (ID of the sampling event, in case more than 1 subsample was collected vertically)\
2) sampleID (ID of individual sample)\
3) origSp - the name as it was given in the source data\
4) valid_name - the name that was identified as valid taxa in World Register of Marine Species (WORMS). NB! Some names may have already changed, due to continuous revision of taxonomy.\
5) AphiaID - WORMS code for the valid name.\
6) cellVol - volume of individual counting unit (cubic micrometers)\
7) UnitsCounted  - the number of cells counted during analysis (mostly missing)\
8) UnitsL  - abundance of counting units (units per litre)\
9) ww - wet weight biovolume (micrograms per litre)\
10) cbl - carbon biomass, micrograms per litre.\
\
sample.table:\
1) sampleID and samplingID - the same as in count.table\
2) lat and lon - the decimal degrees of latitude (N) and longitude (E)\
3) stn - arbitrary code of the sampling station used by data providers.\
4) obstime - date of sampling\
5) minD, maxD - the upper and lower depth of sampling\
6) provider - refers to the institution providing the data (see Table 1 in Olli et al (2013)).\
7) basin and sub basin according to the Helcom classification of Baltic Sea subdivisions, follows usually the bottom topography.\
8) stnDepth - the depth of water at the station\
9) Temp - measured sea surface temperature\
10) Salin - measured sea surface salinity\
11) Ptot - total phosphorus\
12) Ntot - total nitrogen\
13) PO4 - inorganic phosphorus\
14) NO23, NO2, NO3 - inorganic nitrite and nitrate\
15) BSi - biogenic silica\
16) chla - Chl a\
\
phytoplankton.traits:\
1) Aphia - Aphia ID of WORMS\
2) Kingdom \'97 Genus: taxonomy of the taxon, retrieved from WORMS\
3) valid_name - same as in count.table, the currently valid name of species at the time of last update\
4) nfix: N2-fixation ability, binary trait, 1 - present, 0 - absent (same for the following binary traits)\
5) buoyancy: ability to regulate vertical position in the water column (binary)\
6) silica: siliceous cell walls (binary)\
7) motility (binary - ability to move around, with flagella, cilia etc)\
8) autotrophy - ability of autotrophic growth (binary)\
9) heterotrophy - ability of heterotrophic growth (binary, NB! does not exclude autotrophy, if both are 1, species is mixotrophic)\
10) fyco - presence of accessory pigments phycobilins, binary\
11) chlc - presence of accessory pigment chlorophyll c, binary\
12) chlb - presence of accessory pigment chlorophyll b, binary\
13) chain - ability to form chains, filaments or colonies, both facultatively or obligatorily (binary)\
14) mean.vol - mean log-transformed cell volume as reported in data (weighted by the occurrences of different values)\
15) standard deviation of the log-transformed cell volumes as reported in data\
\
